{"path":"ranges/drop_view/begin","title":"std::ranges::drop_view<V>::begin","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::drop_view&lt;V&gt;::</span>begin","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/begin","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Returns an iterator to the first element of the drop_view, that is, an iterator to the Nth element of the underlying view, or to the end of the underlying view if it has less than N elements.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*simple-view*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/random_access_range\"><span class=\"kw2924\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">random_access_range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/sized_range\"><span class=\"kw2918\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">sized_range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/random_access_range\"><span class=\"kw2924\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">random_access_range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/sized_range\"><span class=\"kw2918\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">sized_range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns an iterator to the first element of the <code>drop_view</code>, that is, an iterator to the <i>N</i><sup><i>th</i></sup> element of the underlying view, or to the end of the underlying view if it has less than <i>N</i> elements.\n</p><p>If <code>V</code> is not a <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/random_access_range\"><code>random_access_range</code></a> or a <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/sized_range\"><code>sized_range</code></a>, in order to provide the amortized constant time complexity required by the <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><code>range</code></a> concept, the overload <span class=\"t-v\">(1)</span> caches the result within the <code>drop_view</code> object for use on subsequent calls.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ranges/next\"><span class=\"kw3161\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">next</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, count_, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/end\"><span class=\"kw2902\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">end</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, where <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view#Data_members\"><code><i>base_</i></code></a> is the underlying view, and <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view#Data_members\"><code><i>count_</i></code></a> is the number of elements to skip.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;array&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;concepts&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iterator&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ranges&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> println<span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><span class=\"kw2916\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range</span></span></a> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> range<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> elem <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> range<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> elem<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array\"><span class=\"kw1276\">std::<span class=\"me2\">array</span></span></a> hi<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'H'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'e'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'l'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'l'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'o'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">','</span>, <span class=\"st0\">' '</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'C'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'+'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'+'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'2'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'0'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'!'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    println<span class=\"br0\">(</span>hi<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> pos <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/distance\"><span class=\"kw678\">std::<span class=\"me2\">distance</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>hi.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/find\"><span class=\"kw3002\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">find</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>hi, <span class=\"st0\">'C'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> cxx <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view\"><span class=\"kw2945\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">drop_view</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span>hi, pos<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"*drop_view::begin() == '\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>cxx.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"co1\">//  *cxx.begin() = 'c'; // undefined: 'views' are to be used as observers</span>\n    println<span class=\"br0\">(</span>cxx<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Hello, C++20!\n*drop_view::begin() == 'C'\nC++20!</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3482\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3482</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++20\n</td>\n<td>the const overload can be called with unsized ranges\n</td>\n<td>the const overload requires <code>sized_range</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/end\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>end</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an iterator or a sentinel to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::begin</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> returns an iterator to the beginning of a range<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(customization point object)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/end\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::end</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> returns a sentinel indicating the end of a range<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(customization point object)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/drop_view","title":"std::ranges::views::drop, std::ranges::drop_view"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::drop_view<V>::begin","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Returns an iterator to the first element of the drop_view, that is, an iterator to the Nth element of the underlying…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"ranges::next(ranges::begin(base_), count_, ranges::end(base_)), where base_ is the underlying view, and count_ is the number of elements to skip."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"end","note":"returns an iterator or a sentinel to the end"},{"label":"ranges::begin","note":"returns an iterator to the beginning of a range"},{"label":"ranges::end","note":"returns a sentinel indicating the end of a range"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":295,"codeBlockCount":2}
